{"audit_run_id":"audit:f5b9e1f8a35e4a26acbce9cbd77d5810","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":96,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"Deterministic seeded generator (`SEED = 20260826`, Python `random.Random`). Running it with the"},{"end_column":89,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"project's Python writes `scorpions.csv`. Re-running it reproduces the same file exactly."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"The analysis input. 30 data rows plus one header row. Comma-separated, UTF-8, Unix line endings."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"**What one row represents:** one adult giant hairy scorpion, hand-collected at night under"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"ultraviolet light and measured once in a field laboratory within twelve hours of capture, then"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"released at its capture point. The animal is the unit of the study. Each scorpion appears exactly"},{"end_column":32,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"once. There are no blank cells."},{"end_column":28,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"**Columns, in file order:**"},{"end_column":35,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| Column | Holds | Unit / values |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":105,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `scorpion_id` | Identifier for the individual animal, `SC001` through `SC030` | text, unique per row |"},{"end_column":191,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `group` | Capture site type | text, exactly two values: `burned` (inside the two-year-old burn scar) and `unburned` (adjacent unburned creosote scrub, matched on soil type and elevation) |"},{"end_column":85,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `body_mass_g` | Body mass of the animal at measurement | grams, 2 decimal places |"},{"end_column":135,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `haemolymph_protein_g_l` | Haemolymph total protein concentration from a single haemolymph draw | grams per litre, 1 decimal place |"},{"end_column":158,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| `metabolic_rate_ml_o2_h` | Resting metabolic rate by closed-chamber respirometry at 25 degrees Celsius | millilitres of oxygen per hour, 3 decimal places |"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"The three outcome columns appear in the order the field protocol declared them: body mass, then"},{"end_column":49,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"haemolymph protein, then resting metabolic rate."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"**Row counts:** 15 rows with `group = burned` (`SC001`–`SC015`) and 15 rows with"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"`group = unburned` (`SC016`–`SC030`)."},{"end_column":40,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"**Value ranges in the generated file:**"},{"end_column":31,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"| Column | Minimum | Maximum |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":33,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"| `body_mass_g` | 4.57 | 10.29 |"},{"end_column":43,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"| `haemolymph_protein_g_l` | 31.6 | 67.4 |"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"| `metabolic_rate_ml_o2_h` | 0.073 | 0.252 |"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"These sit inside the typical adult ranges stated in the field protocol: about 3.5 to 11 grams,"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"about 28 to 72 grams per litre, and about 0.04 to 0.32 millilitres of oxygen per hour. The"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":45,"start_column":1,"start_line":45,"text":"generator draws each value from a normal distribution with a per-group mean and standard deviation,"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"redrawing anything that falls outside those hard plausibility limits, so animal-to-animal variation"},{"end_column":67,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"within each site type is realistic and the two site types overlap."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:0560bfc328b29d5bf1e1","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:de87dfac3e7de36bda2b1ada5ecccfca162f2ea536cc0e3e1717d7673caa4011","end_line":47,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-47","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:f5b9e1f8a35e4a26acbce9cbd77d5810","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":86,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"This study compares the two groups recorded in the `group` column of `scorpions.csv`."},{"end_column":119,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"The pre-declared outcome family, in this fixed order, is: body_mass_g, haemolymph_protein_g_l, metabolic_rate_ml_o2_h."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two groups. The named outcomes form one outcome"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"family; per-outcome comparisons over this family require complete-family control of the"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"family-wise error from multiple comparisons."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:62fe682ac2b95cf7f9f7","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:0eb97f0e369ed3e829a81ec73e61546acd4b8850347da041f17d999c15598e07","end_line":7,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-7","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
