{"audit_run_id":"audit:f5b9e1f8a35e4a26acbce9cbd77d5810","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":97,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Thirty adult giant hairy scorpions were hand-collected at night under ultraviolet light: fifteen"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"from inside a burn scar left by a wildfire that ran through creosote scrub two years ago, and"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"fifteen from adjacent unburned scrub matched on soil type and elevation. Each animal was measured"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"once in a field laboratory within twelve hours of capture and then released at its capture point."},{"end_column":37,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"The animal is the unit of the study."},{"end_column":90,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"The field protocol declared three physiological outcomes, in this fixed order: body mass,"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"haemolymph total protein concentration, and resting metabolic rate. Each was declared as a"},{"end_column":27,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"question in its own right."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"The analysis input is `scorpions.csv`: a comma-separated table with one header row and 30 data"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"rows. **One row is one adult scorpion** — one animal, captured once, measured once, released."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"Each scorpion appears exactly once, and every scorpion has a value in every outcome column; there"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"are no blank cells."},{"end_column":28,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"The columns, in file order:"},{"end_column":43,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| Column | What it holds | Unit / values |"},{"end_column":20,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":105,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `scorpion_id` | Identifier for the individual animal, `SC001` through `SC030` | text, unique per row |"},{"end_column":155,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| `group` | Capture site type | text, exactly two values: `burned` (inside the two-year-old burn scar) and `unburned` (adjacent unburned creosote scrub) |"},{"end_column":67,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `body_mass_g` | Body mass of the animal at measurement | grams |"},{"end_column":119,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"| `haemolymph_protein_g_l` | Haemolymph total protein concentration, from a single haemolymph draw | grams per litre |"},{"end_column":128,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"| `metabolic_rate_ml_o2_h` | Resting metabolic rate, by closed-chamber respirometry at 25 °C | millilitres of oxygen per hour |"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"The three outcome columns appear in the order the protocol declared them. The file holds 15 rows"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":33,"start_column":1,"start_line":33,"text":"with `group = burned` (`SC001`–`SC015`) and 15 rows with `group = unburned` (`SC016`–`SC030`)."},{"end_column":92,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"Each declared outcome was compared between the burned and unburned animals with a two-sided"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"Welch's two-sample t-test on the individual animal values (15 animals per site type). Each outcome"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"was judged on its own against the conventional five percent threshold. No multiple-comparison"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"adjustment or correction of any kind was applied. The analysis is reproduced by `analysis.py`."},{"end_column":73,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"Results are given in the order the field protocol declared the outcomes."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"**1. Body mass (g).** Scorpions from the burn scar were lighter: mean 6.45 g in burned scrub"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"against 7.46 g in unburned scrub, a difference of −1.01 g. The difference is statistically"},{"end_column":66,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"significant at the five percent threshold (t = −2.21, p = 0.036)."},{"end_column":87,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"**2. Haemolymph total protein (g/L).** Burned-site animals carried less protein in the"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"haemolymph: mean 43.55 g/L against 53.85 g/L in unburned scrub, a difference of −10.30 g/L. The"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":52,"start_column":1,"start_line":52,"text":"difference is statistically significant at the five percent threshold (t = −4.18, p = 0.00027)."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"**3. Resting metabolic rate (mL O₂/h).** Resting oxygen consumption was slightly higher inside the"},{"end_column":87,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"burn scar: mean 0.186 mL O₂/h against 0.167 mL O₂/h in unburned scrub, a difference of"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"+0.019 mL O₂/h. The difference is not statistically significant at the five percent threshold"},{"end_column":23,"end_line":57,"start_column":1,"start_line":57,"text":"(t = 1.15, p = 0.262)."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"| Outcome | Burned mean | Unburned mean | Difference (burned − unburned) | p | Significant at 0.05 |"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":54,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"| Body mass (g) | 6.45 | 7.46 | −1.01 | 0.036 | yes |"},{"end_column":70,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"| Haemolymph protein (g/L) | 43.55 | 53.85 | −10.30 | 0.00027 | yes |"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":63,"start_column":1,"start_line":63,"text":"| Resting metabolic rate (mL O₂/h) | 0.186 | 0.167 | +0.019 | 0.262 | no |"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"Two years after the fire, scorpions living inside the burn scar are in poorer condition than their"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"neighbours in unburned creosote scrub. They are about a gram lighter on average, roughly a seventh"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":69,"start_column":1,"start_line":69,"text":"of adult body mass, and their haemolymph protein sits about ten grams per litre lower, which is the"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":70,"start_column":1,"start_line":70,"text":"larger and clearer of the two effects and points to a leaner nutritional state rather than simply"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":71,"start_column":1,"start_line":71,"text":"a smaller animal. Resting metabolic rate, by contrast, gives no clear signal: burned-site animals"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"averaged slightly higher oxygen consumption, but the spread among individuals is wide enough that"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"the difference does not separate the two site types at the five percent threshold. On this"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"evidence the burn has cost these scorpions body condition and stored nutrition without any"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"demonstrated shift in their baseline energy use, and the small sample of fifteen animals per site"},{"end_column":56,"end_line":76,"start_column":1,"start_line":76,"text":"leaves the metabolic question open rather than settled."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":78,"start_column":1,"start_line":78,"text":"Next season the team plans to add prey-availability transects and gut-content sampling at the same"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":79,"start_column":1,"start_line":79,"text":"capture points, so that the condition gap can be checked against how much food the burn scar is"},{"end_column":19,"end_line":80,"start_column":1,"start_line":80,"text":"actually offering."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:36252fa269bae857f7aa","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:fc0c79c176da72239e2b5798920b1f66550fdc2bd17e58f3306cf7048ea406d8","end_line":80,"locator":"report.md:1-80","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
